# Serverless Integration Rules

## Import Patterns

### Correct Serverless Imports
Always use `require()` with relative paths for serverless imports:
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Serverless service imports
const PortfolioService = require("../../../../serverless/src/services/portfolio-service");
const TradingService = require("../../../../serverless/src/services/trading-service");
const MarketDataService = require("../../../../serverless/src/services/market-data-service");

// ✅ CORRECT - Serverless utility imports
const Logger = require("../../../../serverless/src/utils/logger");
const ErrorHandler = require("../../../../serverless/src/utils/error-handler");
const Validators = require("../../../../serverless/src/utils/validators");

// ✅ CORRECT - Serverless config imports
const { DYNAMODB_TABLES } = require("../../../../serverless/src/config/constants");
const { getEnvConfig } = require("../../../../serverless/src/config/environment");
```

### Incorrect Imports
Avoid ES6 imports for serverless code:
```typescript
// ❌ AVOID - ES6 imports don't work with serverless Node.js code
import { PortfolioService } from "../../../../serverless/src/services/portfolio-service";

// ❌ AVOID - Relative path issues
const PortfolioService = require("../../../../../serverless/src/services/portfolio-service");
```

## Service Usage Patterns

### Portfolio Service
```typescript
const PortfolioService = require("../../../../serverless/src/services/portfolio-service");

export default async function PortfolioPage() {
  const portfolioService = new PortfolioService();

  try {
    const portfolio = await portfolioService.getCurrentPortfolio();
    return <PortfolioView data={portfolio} />;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Portfolio fetch error:", error);
    return <PortfolioView data={{ totalValue: 0, positions: [] }} />;
  }
}
```

### Trading Service
```typescript
const TradingService = require("../../../../serverless/src/services/trading-service");

export default async function TradingPage() {
  const tradingService = new TradingService();

  try {
    const trades = await tradingService.getRecentTrades();
    return <TradingView trades={trades} />;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Trading fetch error:", error);
    return <TradingView trades={[]} />;
  }
}
```

### Market Data Service
```typescript
const MarketDataService = require("../../../../serverless/src/services/market-data-service");

export default async function MarketPage() {
  const marketDataService = new MarketDataService();

  try {
    const marketData = await marketDataService.getMarketOverview();
    return <MarketView data={marketData} />;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Market data fetch error:", error);
    return <MarketView data={{}} />;
  }
}
```

## Environment Configuration

### Accessing Serverless Environment
```typescript
const { getEnvConfig } = require("../../../../serverless/src/config/environment");

export default async function ConfiguredPage() {
  const envConfig = getEnvConfig();

  // Now you have access to all serverless environment variables
  const aiProvider = envConfig.aiProvider;
  const tradingMode = envConfig.executeTrades ? "live" : "simulation";

  return <ConfigView aiProvider={aiProvider} tradingMode={tradingMode} />;
}
```

## Error Handling

### Database Connection Errors
```typescript
const ErrorHandler = require("../../../../serverless/src/utils/error-handler");

export default async function DataPage() {
  const errorHandler = new ErrorHandler("frontend-data-page");

  try {
    const service = new SomeService();
    const data = await service.getData();
    return <DataView data={data} />;
  } catch (error) {
    // Log error using serverless logger
    console.error("Data fetch error:", error);

    // Return error response using serverless error handler
    return errorHandler.createErrorResponse(error);
  }
}
```

## Logging

### Using Serverless Logger
```typescript
const Logger = require("../../../../serverless/src/utils/logger");

export default async function LoggedPage() {
  const logger = new Logger("frontend-logged-page");

  try {
    logger.info("Starting data fetch");
    const service = new SomeService();
    const data = await service.getData();
    logger.info("Data fetch completed", { count: data.length });

    return <DataView data={data} />;
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error("Data fetch failed", error);
    return <ErrorView />;
  }
}
```

## Validation

### Using Serverless Validators
```typescript
const Validators = require("../../../../serverless/src/utils/validators");

export default async function ValidatedPage() {
  const validators = new Validators();

  // Validate input data
  const isValid = validators.validatePortfolioData(inputData);

  if (!isValid) {
    return <ValidationError />;
  }

  // Proceed with valid data
  const service = new PortfolioService();
  const result = await service.updatePortfolio(inputData);

  return <SuccessView result={result} />;
}
```

## Constants and Configuration

### Using Serverless Constants
```typescript
const { DYNAMODB_TABLES, ITEM_TYPES } = require("../../../../serverless/src/config/constants");

export default async function ConstantsPage() {
  // Access table names
  const tradingTable = DYNAMODB_TABLES.TRADING_TABLE;

  // Access item types
  const portfolioType = ITEM_TYPES.PORTFOLIO;

  // Use in service calls
  const service = new PortfolioService();
  const data = await service.getItemsByType(portfolioType);

  return <ConstantsView data={data} />;
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Import Organization
Group imports by type:
```typescript
// Services
const PortfolioService = require("../../../../serverless/src/services/portfolio-service");
const TradingService = require("../../../../serverless/src/services/trading-service");

// Utilities
const Logger = require("../../../../serverless/src/utils/logger");
const ErrorHandler = require("../../../../serverless/src/utils/error-handler");

// Configuration
const { getEnvConfig } = require("../../../../serverless/src/config/environment");
const { DYNAMODB_TABLES } = require("../../../../serverless/src/config/constants");
```

### 2. Error Handling
Always wrap serverless service calls in try-catch:
```typescript
try {
  const service = new Service();
  const data = await service.method();
  return <SuccessView data={data} />;
} catch (error) {
  console.error("Service error:", error);
  return <FallbackView />;
}
```

### 3. Fallback Data
Provide meaningful fallback data when services fail:
```typescript
let data = { items: [], total: 0 }; // Default structure

try {
  const service = new Service();
  data = await service.getData();
} catch (error) {
  console.error("Service failed:", error);
  // Keep default data structure
}

return <DataView data={data} />;
```

### 4. Type Safety
Create TypeScript interfaces for serverless data:
```typescript
interface PortfolioData {
  totalValue: number;
  positions: Position[];
  lastUpdated: string;
}

interface Position {
  symbol: string;
  shares: number;
  avgPrice: number;
  currentPrice: number;
}
```

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

- ❌ Using ES6 imports for serverless code
- ❌ Not handling service errors gracefully
- ❌ Missing fallback data structures
- ❌ Inconsistent import paths
- ❌ Not using serverless logging utilities
